  "name": "Australian convict and colonial ballads (traditional bush song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Traditional English-language songs of colonial Australia, from transportation and convict ballads such as Jim Jones at Botany Bay and Moreton Bay to bushranger, goldfields, shearing and droving songs, many set to Irish, Scottish and English tunes and handed on orally among bush workers. The goldfields entertainer Charles Thatcher published his songs of the 1850s and 1860s in songsters, and from the 1950s collectors led by John Meredith recorded surviving traditional singers, mostly unaccompanied, in recordings now held by the National Library of Australia; this entry is that sung tradition, not the later bush-band revival.",
